# Accepted findings for `trivy fs` (see .github/workflows/security.yml).
# Every entry says why it is accepted, what would let it be removed, the date
# it was accepted (and last re-checked) and a review date. The dispositions
# are recorded in docs/audit/<date>/ (latest:
# docs/audit/2026-10-22/scanner-triage.md).

# glib 0.18.5, GHSA-wrw7-89jp-8q8g (MEDIUM): unsound VariantStrIter iterator.
# glib arrives only through Tauri's Linux GTK stack (tauri -> muda -> gtk 0.18
# -> glib 0.18), which Tauri pins. The unsound iterator is reached only
# through Variant::array_iter_str, which neither the app nor any crate in
# that stack calls (registry search of every glib dependent in Cargo.lock,
# 2026-10-23; docs/audit/2026-10-22/scanner-triage.md). Remove when Tauri
# moves to gtk-rs 0.20 or later.
# Accepted 2026-10-07; re-checked 2026-10-22 (tauri 2.12.2 still pulls gtk
# 0.18.2 and glib 0.18.5); review by 2027-01-31.
GHSA-wrw7-89jp-8q8g

# rustls-webpki 0.102.8 (GHSA-82j2-j2ch-gfr8 HIGH, GHSA-pwjx-qhcg-rvj4 MEDIUM,
# GHSA-965h-392x-2mh5 LOW, GHSA-xgp8-3hg3-c2mh LOW, CVE-2026-111943 for
# RUSTSEC-2026-0382, distrusted emSign intermediates). Pulled only by rumqttc
# 0.25.1, which pins ^0.102.8; rumqttc uses it for an error type only. The
# IIFL Capital feed hands rumqttc its own rustls 0.23 config, so certificates
# are verified by the patched rustls-webpki 0.103.16 and the 0.102 code never
# runs. Same entries as .github/deny.toml. Remove when rumqttc moves to 0.103.
# CVE-2026-111943 also names RUSTSEC-2026-0381 (webpki-roots), which is fixed
# by webpki-roots 1.0.10, not accepted; cargo-deny and cargo-audit still gate it.
# Accepted 2026-10-08 (CVE-2026-111943: 2026-10-22); re-checked 2026-10-22
# (rumqttc 0.25.1 is still the latest release and its main branch still pins
# 0.102.8); review by 2027-01-31.
GHSA-82j2-j2ch-gfr8
GHSA-pwjx-qhcg-rvj4
GHSA-965h-392x-2mh5
GHSA-xgp8-3hg3-c2mh
CVE-2026-111943
